*******************************
**BEGIN type4052.ddck
*******************************

*****************************************
** Contact person : M. Arenas
** Creation date  : 08.10.2026
** Last changes   : 08.10.2026
*****************************************

***************************************************************************
** Description:
** Water-water heat pump / chiller with the Lorenz model (Type 4052).
** COP = min(COPMax, eta * T_LM_H / (T_LM_H - T_LM_C)), with the log mean temperatures of both sides shifted by the
** approach temperatures DtAppEvap and DtAppCond.
** eta can depend on the lift L = T_LM_H - T_LM_C (K). EtaModel (same numbering as fortrnsys/lib/lorenzEta.f90 and
** ETA_MODELS in heatPumpFitting/yumHeatPump/LorenzFit.py):
**   0 constant eta = a, 1 linear a + b*L, 2 quadratic a + b*L + c*L^2, 3 power a*L^b, 4 logarithmic a + b*ln(L),
**   5 inverse a + b/L, 6 saturation a*(1-exp(-L/b)), 7 ratio a + b*T_LM_C/T_LM_H
** The heat pump data (EtaModel, EtaA, EtaB, EtaC, DtAppEvap, DtAppCond, COPMax, QLoadMin_kW, QLoadMax_kW,
** DTLoadMax) come from a database ddck included before this one with the same "as" name, e.g.
** database/Komotini/Komotini.
** Needs the Type 4052 DLL with the eta models (fortrnsys PR #94: 12 parameters, eta as output 10).
**
** Mode 2 (heating): load = condenser, the type controls the condenser outlet to TWanted.
** Mode 1 (cooling): load = evaporator, the type controls the evaporator outlet to TWanted.
** useMassFlowIn 1: the load is given by the load side mass flow, 0: by QWanted (W).
***************************************************************************

***********************************
** inputs from hydraulic solver
***********************************
EQUATIONS 6
TEvapIn   = @temp(EvapIn)
TCondIn   = @temp(CondIn)
MfrEvapIn = ABS(@mfr(EvapIn))
MfrCondIn = ABS(@mfr(CondIn))
CpEvap    = @cp(EvapIn)*1000   ! J/kgK
CpCond    = @cp(CondIn)*1000   ! J/kgK

***********************************
** outputs to hydraulic solver
***********************************
EQUATIONS 2
@temp(EvapOut) = TEvapOut
@temp(CondOut) = TCondOut

******************************************************************************************
** outputs to energy balance in kWh
******************************************************************************************
EQUATIONS 3
@energy(in, el, HpComp)   = PelComp_kW
@energy(in, heat, HpEvap) = QEvap_kW
@energy(out, heat, HpCond) = QCond_kW

**********************************
** inputs from other ddck
**********************************
EQUATIONS 3
TWanted = $TSetHp      ! wanted outlet temperature on the load side (degC)
QWanted = $QWantedHp   ! wanted load (W), only used with useMassFlowIn = 0
On      = $OnHp        ! activation signal (-)

***********************************
** Definition of the heat pump type
***********************************
CONSTANTS 2
Mode = 2            ! 1: cooling, load on the evaporator. 2: heating, load on the condenser
useMassFlowIn = 1   ! 1: load from the load side mass flow, 0: from QWanted

EQUATIONS 2
QLoadMin = QLoadMin_kW*1000   ! W
QLoadMax = QLoadMax_kW*1000   ! W

UNIT 162 TYPE 4052   ! Lorenz heat pump model
PARAMETERS 12
EtaA            ! 1 Lorenz efficiency, coefficient a of the eta model
CpEvap          ! 2 Specific heat in the evaporator (J/kg/K)
CpCond          ! 3 Specific heat in the condenser (J/kg/K)
DTLoadMax       ! 4 Max delta T on the load side (K)
QLoadMin        ! 5 Min load capacity (W)
QLoadMax        ! 6 Max load capacity (W)
COPMax          ! 7 Max COP
useMassFlowIn   ! 8 1: use the load side mass flow, 0: use QWanted
Mode            ! 9 1: cooling, 2: heating
EtaModel        ! 10 eta model (0-7)
EtaB            ! 11 coefficient b of the eta model
EtaC            ! 12 coefficient c of the eta model (quadratic)
INPUTS 9
TEvapIn         ! 1 Inlet evaporator temperature (degC)
TCondIn         ! 2 Inlet condenser temperature (degC)
DtAppEvap       ! 3 Temperature difference between fluid and refrigerant in the evaporator (K)
DtAppCond       ! 4 Temperature difference between fluid and refrigerant in the condenser (K)
QWanted         ! 5 Wanted load (W)
TWanted         ! 6 Wanted outlet temperature on the load side (degC)
MfrEvapIn       ! 7 Mass flow rate of the evaporator (kg/h)
MfrCondIn       ! 8 Mass flow rate of the condenser (kg/h)
On              ! 9 Activation signal (-)
20 20 5 5 0 20 0 0 0

EQUATIONS 10   ! Heat pump outputs
TEvapOut   = [162,1]
TCondOut   = [162,2]
QEvap_kW   = [162,3]/1000
QCond_kW   = [162,4]/1000
PelComp_kW = [162,5]/1000
Eer        = [162,6]
Cop        = [162,7]
MfrEvap    = [162,8]   ! kg/h
MfrCond    = [162,9]   ! kg/h
EtaLorenz  = [162,10]  ! eta used by the type (-)

***********************************
** Time step printer
***********************************
CONSTANTS 1
unitStepHp = 333

ASSIGN temp\HP_DT.Prt unitStepHp

UNIT 334 TYPE 25
PARAMETERS 10
$dtSim          ! 1 Printing interval
$START          ! 2 Start time
$STOP           ! 3 Stop time
unitStepHp      ! 4 Logical unit
0               ! 5 Units printing mode
0               ! 6 Relative or absolute start time
-1              ! 7 Overwrite or Append
-1              ! 8 Print header
0               ! 9 Delimiter
1               ! 10 Print labels
INPUTS 13
TEvapIn TEvapOut TCondIn TCondOut MfrEvapIn MfrCondIn Cop Eer EtaLorenz QEvap_kW QCond_kW PelComp_kW On
**
TEvapIn TEvapOut TCondIn TCondOut MfrEvapIn MfrCondIn Cop Eer EtaLorenz QEvap_kW QCond_kW PelComp_kW On

***********************************
** Monthly printer
***********************************
CONSTANTS 1
unitMonthlyHp = 335

ASSIGN temp\HP_MO.Prt unitMonthlyHp

UNIT 336 TYPE 46
PARAMETERS 5
unitMonthlyHp   ! 1: Logical unit number, -
-1              ! 2: Logical unit for monthly summaries, -
1               ! 3: Relative or absolute start time
-1              ! 4: Printing & integrating interval, h. -1 for monthly integration
0               ! 5: Number of inputs to avoid integration, -
INPUTS 3
QEvap_kW QCond_kW PelComp_kW
**
QEvap_kW QCond_kW PelComp_kW

*******************************
**END type4052.ddck
*******************************
